    "selection_rule": "Forward keeps the per-K-round service analytic (round bytes at the hardware DRAM capacity plus the pipeline-depth amortized DRAM latency), so the only measured coefficient is the per-CTA fixed span.  Where the free-slope decomposition of this sweep does not reproduce that analytic round, the span is not read off the free intercept.  fixed_span_ns is the mean over the production-density reference group of the launch median minus the measured empty-wave tail and the analytic round service, per resident wave, which makes the Forward expression unbiased over that group.  empty_wave_slot_ns is the slope of the source-exact all-empty early-return prefix launch against its resident wave count.  local_k_round_interval_ns is the reference group's measured per-K-round issue interval, which the sweep shows to be independent of the N extent; it is checked against the architecture-peak BF16 MMA round issue interval for the tile and must not fall below it."
